From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tanjilbhuiyan <tanjilbhuiyan@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 01:44:59 +0600
Subject: [PATCH 13/14] ASoC: samsung: abox: IOMMU fault worker only touches a
 powered ABOX

The fault worker (added for 6.18 when the dump moved out of hard IRQ)
read the ABOX CPU registers and halted the CPU without checking that the
ABOX block was still powered. If the ABOX runtime-suspends between the
fault and the work item, those reads hit a powered-down block and stall
the bus (the freeze class seen in M10.2 A1d2). Its one-shot flag was also
never cleared, so after the DSP restarts a later fault was only logged.

- Hold a runtime-PM reference only if the device is active
  (pm_runtime_get_if_active()) and act only while the CPU is enabled;
  otherwise report the fault without a dump.
- Re-arm the report in abox_enable(), after flushing a pending worker.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: I18f5cbb50ad3ec0938fcf63387cc181bffad0781
---
 sound/soc/samsung/abox/abox.c | 22 +++++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/samsung/abox/abox.c b/sound/soc/samsung/abox/abox.c
index ed88497cc..f216c3d60 100644
--- a/sound/soc/samsung/abox/abox.c
+++ b/sound/soc/samsung/abox/abox.c
@@ -206,9 +206,21 @@ static void abox_iommu_fault_work_func(struct work_struct *work)
 			iommu_fault_work);
 	struct device *dev = &data->pdev->dev;
 
-	abox_dbg_print_gpr(dev, data);
-	abox_cpu_enable(false);
-	dev_err(dev, "ABOX CPU halted after an IOMMU fault\n");
+	/*
+	 * The CPU registers are in the ABOX block: read them only while it is
+	 * powered (a read of a powered-down block stalls the bus). If it was
+	 * suspended meanwhile, the CPU is already stopped.
+	 */
+	if (pm_runtime_get_if_active(dev) <= 0) {
+		dev_err(dev, "IOMMU fault: ABOX off, no register dump\n");
+		return;
+	}
+	if (data->enabled) {
+		abox_dbg_print_gpr(dev, data);
+		abox_cpu_enable(false);
+		dev_err(dev, "ABOX CPU halted after an IOMMU fault\n");
+	}
+	pm_runtime_put(dev);
 }
 
 static void abox_cpu_power(bool on);
@@ -5485,6 +5497,10 @@ static int abox_enable(struct device *dev)
 
 	dev_info(dev, "%s\n", __func__);
 
+	/* A new DSP start gets its own fault report and halt. */
+	cancel_work_sync(&data->iommu_fault_work);
+	data->iommu_fault = false;
+
 	abox_gic_enable_irq(data->dev_gic);
 
 	abox_request_cpu_gear(dev, data, DEFAULT_CPU_GEAR_ID, ABOX_CPU_GEAR_MAX);
